course: dictionary
lesson: 2567
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word deliver is a good example. «You learn your postcode or ZIP code, because it helps letters to be delivered quickly.» Here deliver means to take letters to the right place.
explain: Read this: «They delivered on time.» Deliver does not mean taking anything anywhere. The clue is on time: they kept the promise they made and finished when they said they would. Ask yourself what is being delivered. A parcel, a speech or a promise? The object or the situation tells you the meaning.
explain: Deliver can also mean to give a talk to an audience, as when pupils deliver presentations to the class. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If «take the talk to the class» makes no sense, but «give the talk to the class» does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Deliver is a verb. Its forms are deliver, delivers, delivered and delivering.
fact: «Deliver» means to take letters, parcels or goods to a place or person.
fact: «Deliver» can also mean to give a speech or talk to an audience, or to do what you promised.
fact: «Deliver a baby» means to help a baby be born. Old use: «deliver from danger» means to rescue.
fact: When someone you do not know says they are delivering something, do not open the door. Let an adult deal with them.
exercise: «The postman will deliver the parcel before lunch.» What does deliver mean here? | To throw the parcel away | To hide the parcel under a bush | *To take the parcel to the right place | To open the parcel and read the label
exercise: Maya will deliver a speech to the school assembly. What does deliver mean here? | *To give the speech to the audience | To run around the field | To cook a meal for the class | To post a letter home
exercise: «A van delivers 24 boxes to each of 5 shops.» How many boxes are delivered in all? | 29 | *120 | 115 | 19
test: «They delivered on time, just as they had promised.» What does delivered mean here? | *They kept their promise | They gave a speech | They lost the parcel | They were late
test: Which sentence uses deliver to mean help a baby be born? | Maya will deliver her talk on Friday | *The nurse helped to deliver the baby in the night | The van will deliver the shopping at five | They delivered on time
exam: Jayden says deliver always means taking parcels. Is he right? | Yes, but only when the post office is open | Yes, deliver always means taking parcels to people | No, it means to shout loudly at someone | *No, deliver can also mean giving a speech or keeping a promise, so the words around it show which meaning
